<section class="hero" id="about">
  <span class="eyebrow">Local AI, tested on ordinary hardware</span>
  <h1>We test which local AI models and ComfyUI workflows actually run, then publish the exact configs.</h1>
  <p>A running log of real work: RTX 5070 Ti benchmarks, ComfyUI workflows, and local AI deployments for German and European creators and small businesses. Written as it happens, not as a review.</p>
</section>

<section class="feed" id="log">
  <div class="section-label">Latest entries</div>
  <!-- ENTRIES:TOP -->

  <article class="entry">
    <span class="stamp">planned · infrastructure · part 1 of 2</span>
    <h2>I'm building a 40 GB AI server out of 2014 server parts, and the GPUs are the boring half</h2>
    <div class="meta">25 Aug 2026 · dual Xeon E5-2620 v3 · Supermicro X10DRi-T4+ · 40 GB pooled VRAM</div>
    <p>A third local node built from liquidated 2014 datacenter hardware, for 40 GB of pooled VRAM. The VRAM arithmetic is the part I already know — the slow Xeons, the seam between two different cards, and a 12 MB/s LAN are the parts that decide whether it works.</p>
    <a class="read-more" href="/log/40gb-ai-server-from-2014-parts">Read the full entry →</a>
  </article>

  <article class="entry">
    <span class="stamp">tested · storybook · 16 pages rendered</span>
    <h2>My illustration model rendered photographs, and turning the dial did nothing</h2>
    <div class="meta">5 Aug 2026 · Flux.1-dev fp8 · two stacked LoRAs · RTX 5070 Ti 16 GB</div>
    <p>A trained style LoRA returned photoreal images on scene pages — at character strength 1.0, 0.5 and 0.0 alike. The fix was one prompt clause, not a weight, and it inverts the rule I'd written down the day before.</p>
    <a class="read-more" href="/log/style-lora-rendered-photographs">Read the full entry →</a>
  </article>

  <article class="entry">
    <span class="stamp">tested · localki · pc1 offline</span>
    <h2>Why a tax advisor's Excel habit broke my RAG pipeline</h2>
    <div class="meta">24 Jul 2026 · FastAPI · ChromaDB · Ollama Qwen 2.5 14B</div>
    <p>Six bugs came out of a pilot session. One traced back to a habit that predates the software by a decade, and it was quietly destroying the document structure the whole retrieval pipeline depends on.</p>
    <a class="read-more" href="/log/localki-excel-chunking-bug">Read the full entry →</a>
  </article>

  <article class="entry">
    <span class="stamp">tested · localki · deploy pipeline + font swap</span>
    <h2>Cleaning up 30 dead HTML files taught me more about deploys than the deploy did</h2>
    <div class="meta">23 Jul 2026 · GitHub · Netlify · Continuous Deployment</div>
    <p>LocalKI.de's manual drag-and-drop deploys got replaced with GitHub-to-Netlify continuous deployment — and consolidating the source of truth turned up 30 dead HTML files and a font with unintended right-wing associations in Germany.</p>
    <a class="read-more" href="/log/cleaning-up-30-dead-html-files">Read the full entry →</a>
  </article>

  <article class="entry">
    <span class="stamp">researched · localki / klarverk · not built</span>
    <h2>A client asked if I could train a custom model on their images. I didn't know yet.</h2>
    <div class="meta">21 Jul 2026 · Stable Diffusion LoRA fine-tuning · on-prem</div>
    <p>A client asked about training on their own images instead of the RAG setup. Figuring out whether that's even a real offering, and why per-image pricing is the wrong model for it.</p>
    <a class="read-more" href="/log/should-i-even-offer-lora-training">Read the full entry →</a>
  </article>
